>        Also, I've tried out most of the characters, and read about them in 
>the spoiler from WCST, and elves seem to be by far the most powerful 
>characters, with Valkyries, Samurai, Rogues and Priests following.  Anyway, 
>I was wondering what other people thought of character classes.  

  I've had winning games with W, S, V, B, A, E, and P. I've also had very
good games with H, R and T. I've not had much experience with C or K.

   I recommend the following, in order from best to worst:


SPOILERS FOLLOW, NATURALLY.


























1.   Barbarian. Good fighting skills. Start with food. Can begin with named
     weapon. Poison resistance.

2.   Valkyrie. Gets a +1 long sword and +3 shield (very nice to start with).
     Also starts with food, cold resistance and stealth. 

3.   Samarai. Sometimes gets a blindfold.  S gets good kicking ability which 
     is nice for opening chests.

4.   Wizard. Magic resistance cloak. Lots of nice items to start you off.
     When you get some experience with Elbereth WIZARDS BECOME NO. 1.

5.   Priest. Identify blessed/cursed, but also start with 4 potions of holy
     water. Also good kicking ability. Especially good if you can start with
     a magic marker.

6.   Archeologist. Starts with a tinning kit and a pickaxe both extremely
     useful. Especially the pickaxe for shops.

7.   Elf. Start with some useful intrinsics especially sleep resistance
     and automatic search. Often can start with a blindfold.

8.   Rogue. Underrated character. Often get a blindfold to start, also a 
     lockpick (very nice for chests). Very high dexterity to start.
     Also starts with intrinsic stealth. Having sickness potions identified
     at the start is also very convenient.

9.   Healer. Also not as bad as some would claim. Start with a wand of
     sleep and a stethoscope. You can do well with these if you can find
     some good armor early on. Poison resistance.

10.  Caveman. Not much here but high strength.

11.  Tourist. Pretty poor but the expensive camera is a nice item.

12.  Knight. In my opinion the worst character by quite a bit. Dexterity
     always seems to be very low. Very hard sometimes to hit monsters
     and survive despite starting with the best armor class of all.

>do you have to be a Wizard to cast spells?

  No. But you may need high intelligence to be successful.



